<rml>
<head>
    <link type="text/rcss" href="twitch_fallback.rcss"/>
</head>
<body id="fb-body">
    <!--
      What the Twitch screens show when the UI kit could not start
      (evo_hui_start_failed). Those screens exist only in the kit, so without
      it this plain page stands in for all of them. It says what happened and
      offers Settings (RmlUi has its own) or Quit. The rail is navbar.rml.
      Colours and the focused button are set in
      EvoRmlApp::RenderTwitchFallback; the ones below are the host preview's.
    -->
    <div id="fb-content">
        <img id="fb-mark" src="../icons/icon_app.png"/>
        <div id="fb-app"></div>  <!-- the app's name, from sce_sys/param.json -->
        <div id="fb-title">The screens could not start.</div>
        <div id="fb-message">Close the app and start it again. If it keeps happening, send evo.log to the developer.</div>
        <div id="fb-buttons">
            <div id="fb-btn-0" class="fb-btn">Open Settings</div>
            <div id="fb-btn-1" class="fb-btn">Quit</div>
        </div>
    </div>
</body>
</rml>
